<p>Use this tab to adjust brightness, contrast, saturation, and 
 color balance.</p>
<p>Available functions differ depending on the printer or printer driver 
 you are using.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="preset" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Call Preset</span></p>
<p>Call up the preset color balance.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>When you select the preset and click the <span class="Term-Soft">Call</span> button, the selected color balance is reflected 
 in the image.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="2" class="T1" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Edit Color Balance</span></p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="component" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Setting Method</span></p>
<p>Select a component for adjustment.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>This function is available only if you select 
 <span class="Term-Soft">By Each Component</span> for <span class="Term-Soft">Setting 
 Method</span>.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="before" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Before</span></p>
<p>Displays the image of before color adjustment.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="after" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">After</span></p>
<p>Displays the image of after color adjustment.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="brightness" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Brightness:</span></p>
<p>Specify a value in the spin box to adjust the brightness.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Brightness refers to the brightness of the whole 
 image. Higher brightness levels result in a lighter print image; lower 
 levels, in a darker print image.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="contrast" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Contrast:</span></p>
<p>Specify a value in the spin box to adjust the contrast.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Contrast refers to the relative contrast between 
 light and dark parts of the print image. Higher contrast levels result 
 in a sharper print image; lower levels, in a softer print image.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="saturation" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Saturation:</span></p>
<p>Specify a value in the spin box to adjust the saturation.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Saturation is the purity of a color. Increasing 
 saturation makes a color more vivid, while decreasing saturation makes 
 a color duller.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="adjustment" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Adjust Each Color</span></p>
<p>Specify values in the spin boxes to adjust the color balance of red, 
 green, and blue. </p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="default" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Restore Defaults</span></p>
<p>Restores the settings on this dialog box to the default settings.</p>
